    "DisplayName": "Cumulus humilis",
    "Notes": "Fair-weather cumulus in its flattest form: wider than it is tall, the top barely 400 m above a base on the condensation level. It differs from mediocris in the one number that matters - it stops growing. Placement scale 0.50: fair-weather puffs are half the size of a congestus' patch and there are more of them, which is what 'humilis' describes and what no profile can say.",
